Package: k2
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Wojciech Konsek <33316729+wkonsek@users.noreply.github.com>
Recommends: kubectl
Suggests: vim, jq
Description: terminal UI for working with several Kubernetes clusters side by side
 k2 is a keyboard-driven terminal UI around kubectl: several panes and tabs,
 each with its own kubeconfig, context and namespace, tables, logs,
 describe, port-forwards, kustomize diff/apply and an in-pane vim or shell.
 .
 kubectl is only recommended, not required: it is installed in many ways
 (the Kubernetes apt repository, snap, a download ...).
 .
 On its first start k2 writes the commented example configuration to
 ~/.k2/config.yaml (the package writes nothing into home directories);
 the same file is in /usr/share/k2/config.example.yaml.
